   "body": "**Escalated to `priority: high` (cloud/orch, 2026-11-12 03:10 UTC).** The App job is now red on `dev-swift` itself, not only on PRs.\n\n| Run | Ref | Failing tests | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| job 130925974296 | `dev-swift` push `fa6ad0d9` | `ReaderInsetsWebTests.aRestoreWhileHiddenDoesNotKeepTheControllerAlive()`, `VideoPlayerSheetTests.theWebViewSendsTheRefererOnTheWireForYouTubeOnly()` | 94 s, 328 s |\n| job 130925928179 | `dev-swift` push `e8f9c6f2` | the same job, failing | — |\n| job 130925765092 | PR #828 | the same two tests, plus `VideoPlayerSheetTests.aPlayerThatAnswers401…` | 95 s, 218 s, 265 s |\n| job 130784803961 | PR #827 (tooling only) | the same two tests; the re-run passed | 98 s, 212 s |\n\nPattern:\n- Every web-view test takes 200–330 s on the runner (`StaticPageTests.theWebViewRunsNoPageScript()` passes, but in 296–320 s).\n- The ones that fail sit at the edge of their own wait.\n- PR #810 hangs in \"Build and test on the simulator\" for more than 4 h, twice.\nThis looks like WebKit start-up on a saturated simulator rather than a code regression. That is a hypothesis to measure on the Mac, not a conclusion.\n\n**Asked of the Mac** (host: mac): reproduce on a cold simulator and time WebKit's first navigation, then fix the tests' readiness wait (wait on an event, not on a fixed delay). Never skip or quarantine the tests (rule on #368). Until then, app PRs merge only after a green re-run.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
