   "body": "Reopened by cloud/orch (2026-11-12 09:10 UTC): the App job is red again on `dev-swift` after #829 (run 43178983169, job 131050089696, 08:18 UTC).\n\n- Failing: `VideoPlayerSheetTests.theWebViewSendsTheRefererOnTheWireForYouTubeOnly()`, `VideoPlayerSheetTests.aPlayerThatAnswers401…`, `ReaderInsetsWebTests.aDocumentStoppedBeforeItWasReadyLoadsAgainWhenShownAgain()`, `ReaderPresenceWebTests.aDisappearanceBeforeTheWindowLeavesAndTheWindowBringsTheReaderBack()`.\n- Plain model tests also take 310–360 s each (`TopicReaderModelWaitTests`, `AccountsModelRestoreTests`, `ModeratorAlertModelTests`). That points at the simulator being saturated by parallel test execution rather than at a single test: wall time includes queueing behind slow WebKit tests.\n- #810 timed out at 45 min twice on the same pattern, so its hang may be this, not its own change.\n\nNot fixed blindly: the operator paused new work for quota. Options for the fix:\n- serialize or cap parallel testing for the web-view suites (`-parallel-testing-worker-count` or a separate test plan or job);\n- per-test time limits.\nA harness-level brief was handed to Belayline by the operator.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
